@@ -1338,6 +1338,17 @@ By default, column types are automatically detected for CSV or TSV files - resul
 
 Detected types are only applied when the table is created by the command. Inserting CSV or TSV data into a table that already exists leaves the existing column types unchanged - values are inserted using the table's existing schema.
 
+You can override the type of one or more columns using ``--type column type``. The supported types are ``text``, ``integer``, ``float`` and ``blob``. This option can be repeated:
+
+.. code-block:: bash
+
+    sqlite-utils insert images.db images images.tsv --tsv \
+        --type id integer \
+        --type score float \
+        --type content blob
+
+Explicit types take precedence over automatically detected types and still apply when ``--no-detect-types`` is used. They also apply to existing tables, intentionally transforming the specified columns to the requested types.
+
 For example, given a ``creatures.csv`` file containing this:
 
